          "type": [
            "boolean",
            "null"
          ],
          "description": "Snap to audio samples (audio properties).",
          "default": null
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "prop",
        "keys"
      ],
      "description": "Add or replace keys on one property. `t` = item time, `at` = sequence time; both snap to\nframes. A key's `easing` shapes the move to the next key. Example: `{item, prop:\"opacity\",\nkeys:[{at:\"10s\", value:0, easing:\"ease_out\"}, {at:\"12s\", value:1}]}`.\n\nA static property becomes animated with exactly these keys; a key at an occupied time is\nreplaced; a new key inherits the previous key's easing; `replace` makes the result exactly\nthese keys; `fine` snaps audio properties to samples. `Locked` if the track is locked.",
      "title": "KeyframeSet"
    },
